Subject: [PATCH 09321/11362] Record submission 55625457: first scored run on
 the vLLM NVFP4 backend

Operator-authorised submit of kernel v37 at 2026-08-19T14:26:29Z. The --submit-only path
does not write the reference back to the status file, so it is recorded here by hand along
with the gate result and the caveat the gate printed about itself.

Local gate PASSED: 7 solved, median 1739 actions/solve, 0 timeouts, CORE per-level
efficiency 2.1605 against an identical baseline, bonus solves on cd82/ft09/su15.

The caveat is load-bearing and is recorded rather than summarised away:
proposer_config_mismatch=true. The offline gate sets CARNOT_ARC_DISABLE_INDUCTION=1 and
therefore measures a bare-explorer lower bound with no proposer, while the submitted E3
path leaves that hatch unset and can call LocalGGUFProposer. So the gate confirms no
regression in the EXPLORER and is silent about the induction path -- which is precisely
what this submission changes.

Also records the two scores missing from the file: 0.02 on 2026-08-10 and 0.09 on
2026-08-11, against 0.08 on 2026-07-16.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
